<div class="article-content prose" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);">
  <h2>Step-by-Step Calculation Formula &amp; Worked Example</h2>
  <p>Because Chase enforces 1,000-point blocks, any points below the 1,000 threshold cannot be transferred and remain in your Chase balance:</p>
  
  <div class="formula-box" style="margin: 1.5rem 0; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--ink-2); border-left: 4px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 6px;">
    <div><strong>Transferable Points</strong> = Floor(Total Points ÷ 1,000) × 1,000 (minimum 1,000)</div>
    <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong>United Miles Received</strong> = Transferable Points × 1.0 × (1 + Promotional Bonus %)</div>
    <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong>Points Remaining in Chase</strong> = Total Points - Transferable Points</div>
  </div>

  <h3>Worked Real-World Example</h3>
  <p>Suppose you have <strong>52,400 Chase Ultimate Rewards points</strong>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Eligible Transferable Block</strong>: 52,000 points (rounded down to nearest 1,000).</li>
    <li><strong>Leftover in Chase</strong>: 400 points remain in your Chase account.</li>
    <li><strong>United Miles Credited</strong>: 52,000 MileagePlus miles (at standard 1:1 ratio).</li>
    <li><strong>Estimated Travel Purchasing Power</strong>: At a typical 1.2¢ benchmark valuation, 52,000 United miles represent approximately <strong>$624</strong> in travel value.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Transfer Rules, Fees, and Friction Points</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Excise Fee Offset</strong>: <strong>$0</strong>. Unlike American Express (which charges $0.0006 per point up to $99 to transfer to US domestic airlines), Chase absorbs all federal fees. Transferring to United is completely free.</li>
    <li><strong>Transfer Speed</strong>: Transfers typically process <strong>instantly</strong> (under 5 minutes). Ensure your MileagePlus name matches your Chase account exactly to avoid security delays.</li>
    <li><strong>One-Way Irreversibility</strong>: Once transferred, miles cannot be converted back into Chase Ultimate Rewards points. Always confirm award space on United.com before transferring.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Valuation Trade-Off: Is Transferring Chase Points to United Worth It?</h2>
  <p>Chase Ultimate Rewards points have a baseline market valuation of <strong>1.5¢ per point</strong> due to transfer flexibility. United MileagePlus miles carry an estimated valuation of <strong>1.2¢ per mile</strong> due to dynamic award pricing.</p>
  <p>Transferring is generally <strong>worthwhile</strong> when:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>You are booking a specific United award ticket yielding a CPP higher than 1.5¢ (e.g., saver domestic flights during peak holiday periods or international Star Alliance partner flights).</li>
    <li>You need a small top-off (e.g., transferring 5,000 points) to unlock a high-value award ticket you already have miles for.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Transferring is <strong>not worthwhile</strong> if the award redemption yields less than 1.0¢ per point, as you could redeem points directly for cash back or travel portal bookings at a guaranteed 1.0¢ baseline.</p>

